ZN504XG-D build: skip the ISI transport and ProSLIC SLIC modules.

The board wires a Microsemi Le9643 over ZSI, so en75xx-isi-spi and
en75xx-slic-si3219x (and with them the whole vendor/proslic tree) are
dead build weight and a modern-kernel warning risk.  Comment the two
obj-m lines instead of deleting them so upstream merges stay trivial.

Signed-off-by: ZN504XG-D voice porting project
diff --git a/src/Makefile b/src/Makefile
index b1a8e6a..dc2497c 100644
--- a/src/Makefile
+++ b/src/Makefile
@@ -15,9 +15,12 @@ obj-m += en75xx-lec.o
 obj-m += en75xx-pcm.o
 obj-m += en75xx-voice.o
 obj-m += en75xx-zsi.o
-obj-m += en75xx-isi-spi.o
 obj-m += en75xx-slic-le9642.o
-obj-m += en75xx-slic-si3219x.o
+# ZN504XG-D build: the ISI transport and the ProSLIC SLIC are not wired on
+# this board; skipping them keeps the vendor/proslic tree out of the build.
+# The lines are commented, not deleted, so a merge from upstream stays easy.
+#obj-m += en75xx-isi-spi.o
+#obj-m += en75xx-slic-si3219x.o
 
 en75xx-lec-objs            := ../vendor/oslec/echo.o
 
